    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1293">

                <pb facs="1173" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.74/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania, Servia, and Bulgaria</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 21, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 22, 8 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Bulgarian Government has consented to your telegrams 161 and 165.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1293-f1"/> Einstein expected here to-day. Received telegram
                    from Ambassador Sharp stating Wadsworth started for England same day my telegram
                    reached Paris; he repeated same to American Embassy, London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
